// expect-exit: 0
//
// PROBE 04b — probe 04's EMISSION SHAPE, at a size a machine can afford.
//
// ASKS exactly what probe 04 asks about the emitted artifact, and nothing it
// asks about size: is a module-level `pub fixed` array of small structs emitted
// as an LLVM `constant` rather than a mutable `global`; does it land in
// `.rodata`; and is `llvm.global_ctors` absent, so the program does no startup
// work to build it?
//
// WHY IT EXISTS SEPARATELY. The emission form is a property of HOW THE
// DECLARATION IS LOWERED, not of how large it is: the same code path writes
// three hundred rows and thirty thousand. So the shape can be evidenced at 300
// rows for about a tenth of a second, and it is, because O-N4 makes
// `probe04_big_fixed_table.npk` cost 281 seconds and 30.9 GiB and therefore
// unrepeatable in practice and unrunnable in CI. Probe 04 keeps the SIZE
// question — 30 000 rows really compile, the arithmetic holds at that count —
// and this file keeps the SHAPE question, re-derivable by anybody, any time.
//
// DEPENDS ON THE ANSWER: the same rules as probe 04 — ZONE_MODEL.md Z-7 and
// Z-8, SAFETY.md S-19 (`fixed` module state is read-only memory, no
// initialisation at startup, nothing to leak, nothing to race) and TM-007.
//
// THE EVIDENCE IS COMMITTED, not summarised. `probe04b_emission_shape.txt`
// beside this file holds the exact commands, their exit codes, and the IR and
// `readelf` lines quoted verbatim. Regenerate it with:
//
//     npkc tests/probe/probe04b_emission_shape.npk -o p.ll
//     grep -n 'TRANSITIONS' p.ll | cut -c1-160
//     grep -c 'llvm.global_ctors' p.ll                 # must be 0
//     llc -O0 -filetype=obj -relocation-model=static p.ll -o p.o
//     readelf -sW p.o | grep TRANSITIONS                # section index ...
//     readelf -SW p.o                                   # ... must be .rodata
//
// THE DATA is probe 04's closed form, truncated to 300 rows, so the two files
// agree row for row over their common prefix:
//
//     at_utc[i]     = -2208988800 + i * 604800 + (i % 97) * 3600
//     type_index[i] = i % 13                          for i in 0 .. 299
mod:probe04b_emission_shape;

pub struct:ZoneTransition = { int64:at_utc; int32:type_index; };

